  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nIs a ₱200,000 donation to a friend subject to donor's tax under the TRAIN law?\n\n### Short Answer\nYes, a ₱200,000 donation to a friend is subject to donor's tax under the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion (TRAIN) law.\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\n### Practical Application\nIn practice, the donor must file a donor's tax return and pay the corresponding tax on the donation. The tax rate is progressive, starting at 2% for the first ₱100,000 of the net gifts and increasing for higher amounts. Since the donation amount of ₱200,000 is below the exemption threshold of ₱250,000, it will not incur donor's tax. However, it is essential to report the donation to ensure compliance with tax regulations.",
